<title>USA: Popular Inc files $1 bln shelf of debt, pfd.</title>
<headline>Popular Inc files $1 bln shelf of debt, pfd.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-05-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Popular Inc, Puerto Rico's largest financial institution, filed Monday with the U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission a shelf offering of up to $1 billion in debt securities and preferred shares.</p>
<p>Proceeds from the sale of the securities, which may be issued by Popular International Bank Inc or Popular North America Inc, will be used for general corporate purposes.</p>
<p>No underwriters were named in the filing.</p>
</text>
